But I want to mock out a builtin like Print() !
There's no safe way to do this.
SlangFunctionRegister provides a mechanism, but no way to safely tear down.
_TYPE RegTest Mock Addin may provide a method for SlangX addins, give it a try. See example in Test: LIB COMMOD Copy MktData.
But I want to mock out a UFO !
Have a Look at: Mocking a UFO.
You can use _UT Unit Tests For UFO for a quick generation of unit tests.
Alternatively, you can use DefineClass in your test.
But I want to mock out a Typed Structure instance!
See: Example: Moxie TS Test.

Mock interfaces or concrete types like so:


 // quick example
 Moxie = Moxie::Typed Structure( Target Type := "Example::Some Mockable TS"  )
         .Call( "Method", "Argument one", Argument Two := 2 )   .Returning( ["returnvalue"] );

 // do something with this instance - it will be refcounted if the target type is:
 Mock = Moxie.Get Mock();

 // note that you can set member variables in the Get Mock call, like
 Mock With Vars Set = Moxie.Get Mock( Member Var Name := "the value" );

 // check the instance's Method() function was called:
 Moxie.Verify();
 Moxie.Clean Up();
How should I mock out @Config::Load ?
Typically, it will be enough to avoid mocking of any kind and just do


 @Config::Load and Override( "_CFG X", {|Override|}, );
In case the code under test uses Reload := True or Include, you can also do this with RegTestStubConfig: eg

   Link( "_Slang RegTest Stub Function" );
   RegTestStubConfig( Structure(
           "_CFG X", {| a:= 1|},
           "_CFG Y", {| b:= 2|},
   ) )
   {
       @Config::Load( "_CFG X", ReallyReload := True ).a; // will equal 1
   }
RegTestStubConfig may be nested.

I'm using FasTest. Do I have to wrap every test with RegTestStubFunction?
No you can define a test wrapper that's invoked with each test like this:


 /****************************************************************
 **  Routine: Private::Dont Send Notifications And Mock Config Wrapper
 **
 **  Wrap the tests with a RegTestStub to not send notifications
 **  and to mock the config
 ****************************************************************/
 Private::Dont Send Notifications Wrapper = Func(
     Slang( Test Func )
 )
 Returns( Slang() )
 {
     Wrapped Func = Lambda()
     // Notifications
     RegTestStubFunction( Structure(
         "ScriptReview::Send Notification"           , True,
         "MetaProjectScript::Get Scripts For Project", Private::MetaProject Config.Scripts,
     ) )
         @Test Func(); // The test

     Return( Wrapped Func );
 };
Then declare each test to be wrapped by this wrapper in the test function header using 'Fastest-wrap-with':


 /****************************************************************
 **  Routine: Private::Test ScriptReview Has Matching Comment
 **
 **  Fastest-wrap-with: Private::Dont Send Notifications Wrapper
 ****************************************************************/
 Private::Test ScriptReview Has Matching Comment = Func(
 )
 Returns()
 {
     ...etc.